/* func_level_5_8007B68C (0x8007B68C, level_5_artisans_sunny_flight overlay).
 *
 * Flight-level end-of-run results/time-attack screen draw. First frame
 * (D_800758B8 == 0): runs the render pipeline once, then captures the frame
 * into VRAM strips (4x MoveImage columns + LoadImage of the backdrop strip
 * and CLUT row). Later frames: rebuilds the frozen backdrop as 4 POLY_FT4
 * quads (clut 0x3820) plus a black TILE bar, then draws either the results
 * board (COMPLETED/QUIT/TIME IS UP/CRASHED headline, four tally rows
 * revealed by D_80075744, bonus column, TOTAL, PRESS-TO-CONTINUE or
 * TRY AGAIN?/YES/NO menu) or, at D_80075744 == 0x64, the TIME ATTACK board
 * (times via the formatter D_800758C4, NEW RECORD, TRY AGAIN/YES/NO).
 * Selected records get a sine glow on +0x46 from D_8006CC78. Standard
 * 2-vblank pace tail. Word-identical in all five flight overlays (x5 payoff:
 * 32,200 bytes).
 *
 * B14 RETIRED 2026-08-06-1 — the "+1 nop / cannot link" blocker is GONE and
 * this now builds LENGTH-EXACT (1610/1610) and LINKS. The old note said sched1
 * "canonicalizes the three dep-free la insns to fixed positions"; the sched1
 * dump (`cc1 -dS`, `<in>.i.sched`) says otherwise. All three defs
 * (`la envBase`, `la img`, `addiu img2`) carry priority == 1 and are ready from
 * T-1, so they are pure stragglers: they get picked only at scheduling BUBBLES,
 * and `rank_for_schedule` breaks the priority tie on INSN_LUID **descending**,
 * i.e. on SOURCE ORDER. Whichever of them has the highest LUID fills the first
 * bubble. With the original source order (envBase, img, img2) `img2` won the
 * bubble at T-17 and was placed ~11 insns too late, which left PutDrawEnv's
 * delay slot empty. Permuting the three assignment statements to
 * (img, img2, envBase) makes `envBase` take that bubble instead; `img2` then
 * falls to the next one, which is the slot immediately before the PutDrawEnv
 * call, and reorg eats it into the delay slot exactly as the original does.
 * The earlier "statement position" probes moved ONE statement at a time and so
 * never changed the relative LUID order, which is the only thing that matters.
 * Remaining residue (content-aligned MISMATCH 75/1610 as of 2026-08-18; the linked diff
 * is positionally phase-shifted by the one insn below and reads far worse than
 * the function really is): `la envBase` still lands ~20 insns late (it takes
 * the T-17 bubble; the original has it before the FIRST PutDispEnv), a +8 frame
 * (A127), the else-arm `move s5,zero` bne delay slot, and the old list -
 * quad-loop temp register roles
 * (a/bh/ch/d land a1/a0/a1/v0 vs orig v0/a1/a2/v1, tpage t0 vs a3),
 * YES/NO blink blocks (orig holds &pos in s2 across the cse jump-follow
 * path and loads D_80075720 between the pos stores), publish-loop
 * slot/r register mirror, init-arm i++/lw ordering. All solved recipes and
 * the exact orig dataflow are in cookbook AD; everything else - including
 * all 5 tally stanzas, TOTAL, PRESS block, time-attack board, all string
 * literals (owned .rodata, emitted in use order), memcpy message copies,
 * record block, pace tail - is byte-identical.
 *
 * 2026-07-25-1 unattended permuter session (~15m, ~16000 iterations — a slow,
 * large function — timed out at the 15m budget): best score 3000 vs base score
 * 3705, across 143 output dirs. No byte-perfect candidate found; still PARKED.
 *
 * 2026-08-06-2 — FULL RESIDUE INVENTORY (content-aligned masked diff, 78/1610).
 * Drive this park off the content-aligned diff, never the linked one: the
 * linked diff reads 1341/1610 because the `la envBase` displacement phase-shifts
 * everything after insn 25. Recipe (~10 s/iteration): `open-spyro diff <fn>`,
 * then objdump both `build/diff/<fn>.{orig,built}.bin` with
 * `-b binary -m mips:3000 -EL -D`, anchor register names
 * (`\b(a[0-3]|v[01]|t[0-9]|s[0-8]|at|gp|sp|fp|ra|zero)\b` -> `R\1`), mask
 * immediates, and difflib-align. Thirteen INDEPENDENT residues, by orig insn:
 *   R1  25/26   `la envBase` lands at 45/46 instead of 25/26 (4 insns).
 *   R2  70      `i += 1` (2).      R3  82-88  rect.x/rect.y store vs `lw a1,0(s3)`
 *               ordering (6).
 *   R4  119     else-arm `move s5,zero` in the `bne` delay slot (1-2).
 *   R5  126     `ori a1,a1,0x3e00` emitted 4 insns late (2).
 *   R6  144     tpage `addiu a3,s1,136` lands in t0 (1) + the `sll x` position.
 *   R7  159-200 the quad-loop temp register roles — a/bh/ch/d take a1/a0/a1/v0
 *               where the orig has v0/a1/a2/v1 (~25 insns, the big one).
 *   R8  1067-74 v0/v1 mirror + `move a1,s2` position (5).
 *   R9  1090-1124 `addiu a1,sp,56` (&pos) placement in the YES/NO blink blocks
 *               and the `move a3,zero` it displaces (5).
 *   R10 1138-41, R12 1355-58 + 1403-06  `move a0,zero` one slot early (6 total).
 *   R11 1158-71 publish-loop `la`/cursor register mirror (~10).
 *   R13 1432-34 orig holds `&pos` in s2 (`addiu s2,sp,56; move a1,s2`); ours
 *               recomputes `addiu a1,sp,56` per site — this is A26 (a distinct
 *               SCALAR alias for the cross-call address), untried here.
 *   +   frame is `addiu sp,-152` vs the orig's `-144`: exactly ONE extra 8-byte
 *       spill slot (A127; saved-reg region and the 52 B of declared aggregates
 *       already agree). This is invisible to the masked diff but costs 14
 *       sp-relative immediates; the other 79 immediate-only diffs are branch
 *       and `j` targets that fall out with the shape.
 * Findings this session:
 *  - **The permuter body's `allclear = 0x15;` hack is LOAD-BEARING.** Replacing
 *    `*(p + allclear) = bq;` with the literal `*(p + 0x15) = bq;` (and dropping
 *    the assignment) is the "clean" form and makes it WORSE, 78 -> 85: the
 *    `li s5,21` is what holds the slot at orig 169 that `addiu s1,s1,1` wants,
 *    and removing it lets `x = i << 7` sink from 143 to 155 and kills the
 *    `move s5,zero` delay-slot fill at 119 (it becomes dead, since s5 is then
 *    unconditionally re-set in the loop). Do not "clean up" R2/R4 in isolation.
 *  - The hand-written body (git show 46305b0:...) plus the A164 permutation is
 *    85/1610 — 7 WORSE than this permuter body, and it adds two new residues
 *    (a second `la D_80076EE0` at 114/115 and the `sll v1,s1,0x7` position).
 *    The permuter body is the better base; keep it.
 *  - **R1 is now fully probed: all three legal source orders are known.**
 *    `img2 = img - 2` cannot precede `img`, so only (envBase,img,img2),
 *    (img,envBase,img2) and (img,img2,envBase) exist. (envBase,img,img2) =
 *    +1 insn, cannot link (the old B14 state). (img,envBase,img2) = +1 insn,
 *    cannot link (NEW, measured 2026-08-06-2). (img,img2,envBase) = current.
 *    A164 has nothing left to give here; R1 needs a different mechanism.
 *  - The quad block's u/v byte writes carry a mode residue the masked diff
 *    HIDES: orig has `addiu v0,v0,128` for `u1 = u0 + 0x80` / `u3 = u0 + 0x80`
 *    (SImode), ours has `addiu v0,v0,-128` (combine narrowed the `plus` to
 *    QImode against the `sb`). The neighbouring `v2/v3 = v0coord - 0x21` gives
 *    `addiu -33` on BOTH sides, so the original's source really does write
 *    `- 0x21` and `+ 0x80` and keeps both in SImode. Fixing this (A116's
 *    inverse) is worth 2 more bytes and may be a lever on R7.
 * 2026-08-18 — R9/R13 SOLVED for the results board; 78/1610 -> 75/1610
 * (46 regions). The a1 = &pos arg setup that ours rematerialised in the block
 * immediately before each `func_80017FE4` call is, in the original, the DEF of
 * an explicit pointer local written between the pos[] stores and the blink
 * `if`. Writing `int *pp; ... pos[0]=..; pos[1]=..; pos[2]=..; pp = pos;
 * if (blink test) ...; func_80017FE4("YES", pp, ...)` puts the copy where the
 * original has it (`move a1,s2` at orig 1071) and lets the NO block's
 * rematerialised `addiu a1,sp,56` fall into the `bne` delay slot at orig 1108.
 * Both YES/NO blocks of the RESULTS board now match; the pointer local costs
 * nothing there because `pos` is already carried in s2.
 * The TIME-ATTACK board wants the same shape and it is now measured, not
 * guessed: orig 1432 opens it with `addiu s2,sp,56; move a1,s2` (a FRESH
 * carrier established at the "TRY AGAIN" call, then reused by `move a1,s2` at
 * 1448 and rematerialised at 1485), i.e. a second pointer local scoped to that
 * branch. Every spelling of that (`int *pp` block-local, `int *pp` at else
 * scope, reusing the dead `fp`, and each of TRY-AGAIN/YES/NO alone) compiles to
 * 1611 insns and CANNOT LINK — exactly +1. Use the compile-only insn count
 * (`config/compile.sh ovl <src> /tmp/g.o` + `objdump -d | grep -c` = 1610 for a
 * linkable body) to iterate there; the +1 has to be paid back by fixing one of
 * R10/R11/R12 in the same pass, so do NOT attempt the time-attack carrier on
